1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:01,860
Two minutes past 10 in the morning,

2
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:04,440
the 11th of September, 2001.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:09,020
On an open line between the Federal Aviation Administration's command center and its

4
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:13,020
headquarters, a controller says something out loud that he probably should not have had

5
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:16,140
to say. Air Force One, he says,

6
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:17,960
still does not have a fighter escort.

7
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:20,800
The voice at headquarters answers,

8
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,000
they still do not? Holy cow.

9
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,440
The President of the United States had been in the air for seven minutes.

10
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,820
He would be alone up there for about 95.

11
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:32,900
And in a bunker underneath the White House,

12
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:37,080
a man who was not in the military chain of command was about to give an order to shoot

13
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:38,460
down a passenger aeroplane.

14
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:43,320
Black Box Breakdown. Air Force One,

15
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:47,700
95 minutes alone. Sarasota,

16
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:51,500
Florida. At 32 minutes past eight,

17
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:54,360
the President leaves a beach resort for an elementary school.

18
00:00:54,770 --> 00:00:58,380
He is going to read with second graders and talk about a new education program.

19
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:00,180
On the scale of a presidency,

20
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,440
this is a day nobody would have remembered.

21
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:05,360
At 46 minutes past eight,

22
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:08,120
American Airlines Flight 11 hits the North Tower.

23
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:13,260
The board's finding on what the President's party knew at that moment is one sentence,

24
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,080
and it is worth hearing exactly.

25
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:18,980
No one in the White House or traveling with the President knew that it had been hijacked.

26
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:25,180
Outside the classroom, Carl Rove tells the President a small twin engine plane has crashed

27
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:26,360
into the World Trade Center.

28
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:27,880
The President's reaction,

29
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:32,040
the report says, was that the incident must have been caused by pilot error.

30
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:35,380
He speaks to Condoleezza Rice by phone.

31
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:37,700
She tells him that is all we know right now,

32
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:41,180
Mr. President. At three minutes past nine,

33
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:44,440
United Airlines Flight 175 hits the South Tower.

34
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:50,000
Two minutes later, the White House Chief of Staff walks into a classroom of seven year

35
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,020
olds and leans down to the President's ear.

36
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,940
A second plane hit the second tower.

37
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:59,200
America is under attack, and then nothing happens.

38
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:01,000
The board records it plainly.

39
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:04,880
The President remained in the classroom for another five to seven minutes,

40
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:06,540
while the children continued reading.

41
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:10,920
There is an argument about those minutes that has run for 25 years,

42
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:13,000
and this film is not going to settle it.

43
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,140
What matters for what comes next is what the board found about the information reaching

44
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:22,520
him. No one in the traveling party had any information during this time that other aircraft

45
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,720
were hijacked or missing.

46
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:28,500
At about half past nine, he makes a short statement in the school hall,

47
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,600
and the country hears its President for the first time that morning.

48
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,840
Today, we've had a national tragedy.

49
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:41,080
At 33 minutes past nine, the tower at Reagan National Telephone's the Secret Service

50
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,500
with a sentence that changes the shape of the day.

51
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,780
An aircraft is coming at you and not talking with us.

52
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:49,900
At about 35 minutes past nine,

53
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:51,320
the motorcade leaves the school.

54
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:54,340
The President learns about the Pentagon during the drive.

55
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:58,700
At 37 minutes and 46 seconds past nine,

56
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:00,740
American 77 hits the Pentagon.

57
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:03,760
The plane with no destination.

58
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,180
At about 45 minutes past nine,

59
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:10,360
the President boards. He asks first whether his family is safe.

60
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:12,160
Then he calls the Vice President.

61
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:15,460
Ari Fleischer, the press secretary,

62
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,480
is taking notes by hand all day,

63
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,780
and those notes are one of the few contemporaneous records of what was said.

64
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:24,260
At about 945, the President tells the Vice President this.

65
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:27,600
Sounds like we have a minor war going on here.

66
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:29,200
I heard about the Pentagon.

67
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,600
We're at war, somebody's gonna pay.

68
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,120
Hold that call in your mind,

69
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,720
because it becomes important later.

70
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:38,640
There is no mention in it of shooting anything down.

71
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:43,100
Just before five to ten, Air Force One leaves Sarasota.

72
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,380
The board's phrase for where it was going is three words long,

73
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:48,500
without any fixed destination.

74
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:54,060
A small honesty note. The report gives two different times for that departure in two

75
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,960
different chapters. Chapter one says about 954.

76
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:59,880
Chapter ten says airborne at 955.

77
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,980
We will say just before five to ten and leave it there.

78
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:06,060
The pilot, Colonel Mark Tillman,

79
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:10,260
took off steeply and turned the aircraft away from a reported figure near the runway.

80
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:13,040
It later turned out to be a man with a camera.

81
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:17,860
That detail comes from the pilot's own account rather than the accident record,

82
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:21,580
and we flag it as such. The man was never publicly identified.

83
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,400
Nine minutes before they left,

84
00:04:24,860 --> 00:04:28,780
the North American Aerospace Defense Command had directed every air sovereignty aircraft

85
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:30,040
it had to battle stations,

86
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:35,620
fully armed. And at 959, an Air Force Lieutenant Colonel in

87
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:39,380
the White House Military Office asked the Air Threat Conference for three things.

88
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,080
Continuity of government measures.

89
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,500
A fighter combat air patrol over Washington.

90
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:46,720
And fighter escorts for Air Force One.

91
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,800
The request was made at 959.

92
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,580
The escort arrived at about half past 11.

93
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:57,620
Alone. For roughly an hour and a half,

94
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:01,640
the aircraft carrying the President of the United States flew through American airspace

95
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:03,380
with no fighter alongside it.

96
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:06,640
That is the exchange this film opened on.

97
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:09,180
Two minutes past ten, an FAA line,

98
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:13,220
one controller telling another that Air Force One still does not have a fighter escort.

99
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,700
They still do not? Holy cow,

100
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:19,560
is the National Military Command Center aware of this?

101
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:23,920
One correction to something you will hear repeated about that clip.

102
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,880
It is not a military tape.

103
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:30,640
It is a telephone line between the Federal Aviation Administration's Command Center and

104
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:34,940
its own headquarters. The aircraft climbed high and,

105
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:38,720
at about ten past ten, turned and began heading due west,

106
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:44,080
away from Washington. You will often hear that it climbed to 45 ,000

107
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:47,300
feet. We could not trace that number to any primary source.

108
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:51,060
The radar reconstruction puts it closer to 39 ,000.

109
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:54,700
The plane also had a problem nobody had planned for.

110
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:56,360
Its telephones kept dropping.

111
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,380
The communications networks that morning were at their limit,

112
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:01,440
and Air Force One was not an exception.

113
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:06,780
The bunker. Underneath the east wing of the White House,

114
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,280
there is a shelter conference room.

115
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:11,360
The Vice President reached it at about two minutes to ten.

116
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:17,140
At two minutes past ten, the shelter starts receiving secret service reports of an aircraft

117
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:20,860
inbound to Washington. It is United 93,

118
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:22,900
and the reports are not radar.

119
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:25,460
They are based on a projected flight path.

120
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,920
At three minutes and 11 seconds past ten,

121
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:31,800
United 93 goes into a field in Pennsylvania.

122
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:35,720
Everyone in that bunker is now tracking a plane that no longer exists.

123
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:39,400
Between ten past ten and a quarter past,

124
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:43,600
a military aide comes into the room and says the aircraft is 80 miles out.

125
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:46,340
He asks whether the fighters have authority to engage.

126
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,140
The Vice President says yes.

127
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:50,760
One of the men in the room,

128
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:54,140
Scooter Libby, later described how long the decision took.

129
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:57,160
In about the time, it takes a batter to decide to swing.

130
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,060
A few minutes later, the aide is back,

131
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:02,400
60 miles out. He asks again.

132
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,460
The Vice President says yes again.

133
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,640
Libby was writing it down as it happened.

134
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:11,660
His note is the single best piece of paper we have from inside that room.

135
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:16,200
10, 15 to 18, aircraft 60 miles out,

136
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,200
confirmed as hijack. Engage,

137
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:23,100
VP, yes. And then the last line of that note,

138
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:25,320
which is the reason this episode exists.

139
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:29,800
JB, get president and confirm engage order.

140
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:34,220
JB is Joshua Bolton, the deputy chief of staff.

141
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:35,920
He had been sitting there listening.

142
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:38,300
After what the report calls a quiet moment,

143
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:41,760
he suggested the Vice President call the president and confirm the order.

144
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,540
Think about what that request means.

145
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:48,640
A man in the room believed the order that had just been given needed confirming from

146
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:53,680
someone else, because the Vice President of the United States is not in the military

147
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:58,700
chain of command. The chain runs from the President to the Secretary of Defense

148
00:07:58,700 --> 00:07:59,980
to the combatant commander,

149
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,740
not through the Vice President.

150
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:04,420
The report states it plainly on page 43.

151
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:07,120
The Secretary of Defense,

152
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:09,380
Donald Rumsfeld, was at the Pentagon.

153
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:11,600
The Pentagon had just been hit.

154
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:14,040
He was outside, helping with the wounded.

155
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:19,620
At 18 minutes past 10, the logs show the Vice President calling the President.

156
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,620
A two minute call that, in the board's words,

157
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:24,020
obtained the confirmation.

158
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:29,580
Two minutes after that, Fleischer writes in his notebook that the President had authorized

159
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:31,520
a shoot down of aircraft if necessary.

160
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,820
And the board adds one sentence about that note,

161
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,120
which does a great deal of work.

162
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:39,760
Fleischer's 10 -20 note is the first mention of shoot down authority.

163
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:43,540
The first, not a record of an earlier decision.

164
00:08:44,140 --> 00:08:46,620
The first, which matters,

165
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:50,080
because the Vice President has always said he was not making that decision.

166
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:53,880
He has said the President had already authorized it in an earlier call.

167
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:57,340
So the board went looking for that earlier call.

168
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:59,880
Here's what they found, and this is verbatim.

169
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:05,520
We believe this call would have taken place sometime before 10 -10 -10 -15.

170
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:09,020
Among the sources that reflect other important events of that morning,

171
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:11,520
there is no documentary evidence for this call.

172
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:14,540
And then the part that is rarely quoted.

173
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:16,920
Others nearby who were taking notes,

174
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,660
such as Scooter Libby and Mrs.

175
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:20,420
Cheney, did not note a call.

176
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:25,500
The same man whose handwriting gives us the clearest record of the order recorded no

177
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,120
earlier call authorizing it.

178
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,900
Neither did the Vice President's wife,

179
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:30,920
sitting beside him, also writing.

180
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:34,160
The board does not call anyone a liar.

181
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:36,340
It says the sources are incomplete.

182
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:40,440
We will do the same. What can be said is that the paper does not show what it would need

183
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:45,500
to show. Down the chain. So an order exists.

184
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:47,700
The question is, what happened to it?

185
00:09:48,940 --> 00:09:54,360
At 31 minutes past 10, a message goes out over the North American Aerospace Defense Command's

186
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:57,680
internal chat system. 10 -31.

187
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:01,900
Vice President has cleared to us to intercept tracks of interest and shoot them down

188
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:04,100
if they do not respond, per General Arnold.

189
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:08,780
That is the first time the shoot -down authority reaches the people who would have to

190
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:14,200
carry it out. United 93 had crashed at 3 minutes and 11 seconds

191
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:19,060
past 10. The order arrived 28 minutes after the aeroplane it concerned was already in

192
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:22,720
the ground. And it still did not reach the pilots.

193
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:26,520
The fighters over Washington that morning were from Langley.

194
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:28,320
What they were actually told,

195
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:30,060
in the board's own words,

196
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:35,740
was this. The only orders actually conveyed to the pilots were to identify type

197
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:39,140
and tail. Identify type and tail.

198
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,520
Go and look at it and tell us what it is.

199
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,360
At 10 past 10, those pilots had been told,

200
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:47,140
in writing, negative clearance to shoot.

201
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:50,800
And then the finding this whole film has been walking towards,

202
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:56,220
on page 44. The Vice President was mistaken in his belief that shoot -down

203
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:58,120
authorization had been passed to the pilots.

204
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:01,960
He thought he had given an order that was being carried out.

205
00:11:02,580 --> 00:11:04,080
It was not being carried out.

206
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,100
Nobody in a cockpit had been told.

207
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:09,100
And while that order was going nowhere,

208
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:11,800
something else was happening at Andrews Air Force Base,

209
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:13,260
10 miles from the Capitol.

210
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:17,900
The District of Columbia Air National Guard was putting fighters into the air.

211
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:19,980
Not because NORAD told them to.

212
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:22,900
Because the Secret Service picked up a phone and asked.

213
00:11:24,580 --> 00:11:27,940
The board's finding on that launch is as stark as the one about the Vice President.

214
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:31,380
Those aircraft went up outside the military chain of command.

215
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:34,380
NORAD did not know they were up.

216
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,020
The National Military Command Center did not know.

217
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:38,740
The President did not know.

218
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:40,540
The Vice President did not know.

219
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:44,820
The first of them was airborne at 38 minutes past 10.

220
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:48,460
So hold the two halves of this next to each other.

221
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:51,020
In a bunker, an order to engage,

222
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:53,020
given by a man outside the chain,

223
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:56,400
reaching no pilot. Over Washington,

224
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:59,180
pilots in the air launched outside the chain,

225
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:01,180
who the chain did not know were there.

226
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:04,140
Two failures of the same system,

227
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:07,120
running in opposite directions in the same 20 minutes.

228
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:13,380
At 39 minutes past 10, the Vice President and the Secretary of Defense finally speak.

229
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:16,720
And the transcript of that call is the whole morning in miniature.

230
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:21,540
The Vice President says they have already taken a couple of aircraft out.

231
00:12:22,660 --> 00:12:26,160
They had not. The board's next paragraph says he was mistaken.

232
00:12:26,860 --> 00:12:28,820
No aircraft had been engaged by anyone.

233
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:31,420
By the end of that same call,

234
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:34,240
he says it himself. We can't confirm that.

235
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:36,480
We're told that one aircraft is down,

236
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,680
but we do not have a pilot report that did it.

237
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:43,520
There is one more moment in that bunker that says everything about the information they

238
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:46,720
were working from. At about half past 10,

239
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:50,060
another report comes in. Another hijacked aircraft,

240
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:55,120
5 to 10 miles out. The Vice President authorizes engagement again.

241
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:59,340
Take it out. It was a medical evacuation helicopter.

242
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:03,820
Nothing happened to it, because the order had nowhere to go.

243
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:07,620
That is the only reason. One aircraft was down.

244
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:09,460
40 people had put it there.

245
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:15,940
The claim. There is a version of this story that says the order was carried out,

246
00:13:16,180 --> 00:13:18,120
that United 93 was shot down,

247
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,700
and that the passenger revolt is the cover story.

248
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,440
It is worth stating fairly,

249
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:25,160
because it is not made of nothing.

250
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:28,900
Its supporters point to debris found well away from the crash site,

251
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:31,140
to witnesses who described a second aircraft,

252
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:34,440
and to the Vice President's own ambiguous remarks that morning.

253
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,860
So let us test it, plank by plank,

254
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:40,580
against the record. First,

255
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:45,340
the order reached the North American Aerospace Defense Command at 31 minutes past 10.

256
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:48,220
The airplane hit the ground at 3 minutes past 10.

257
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:51,920
An order that arrives 28 minutes late cannot have been executed.

258
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,940
Second, the pilots were never told to shoot.

259
00:13:56,340 --> 00:14:00,560
The board is explicit. The only orders actually conveyed to them were to identify type

260
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:04,640
and tail. Third, and this is the one that ends it,

261
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:09,980
the defense sector responsible did not know United 93 existed until after it had crashed.

262
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,440
They first heard of it at 7 minutes past 10,

263
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:15,860
from a civilian center's military liaison,

264
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:18,140
4 minutes after it was already down.

265
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:23,800
The command had originally told investigators it had been tracking the flight since 916.

266
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:26,340
That timeline turned out to be false.

267
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:32,380
The board said so. You cannot shoot down an aircraft you have not been told about,

268
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:34,260
with an order that has not arrived,

269
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:36,900
using pilots who were told to identify it.

270
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:39,300
And there is one more line,

271
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:42,160
endlessly quoted by people arguing for the shoot down,

272
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:44,680
which says the opposite of what they think it says.

273
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:49,660
NORAD officials have maintained that they would have intercepted and shot down United

274
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:53,820
93. We are not so sure. Read it again.

275
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:56,620
The board is not doubting the official story.

276
00:14:57,200 --> 00:15:00,720
The board is doubting the military's claim that it could have stopped the plane at all.

277
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:04,280
And all 44 people aboard were identified.

278
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,580
Fingerprints, dental records,

279
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,720
and DNA overseen by the county coroner.

280
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:13,860
33 passengers, 7 crew, and 4 hijackers.

281
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:18,420
Angel Around half past 10,

282
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:21,240
a warning spreads through the bunker and onto the aeroplane.

283
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,580
A call had come into the White House switchboard.

284
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:28,860
Angel is next. Angel was the internal call sign for Air Force One,

285
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:32,100
and it was not public. Which meant,

286
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:35,920
to the people on board, that whoever made that call knew something they should not have

287
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:39,000
known. Agents were posted in the aisle and at the cockpit door.

288
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:42,000
Here's what the record actually says,

289
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:45,020
and it is more complicated than the version you usually hear.

290
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:50,240
The report describes a reported threat to Angel that originated in a misunderstanding

291
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,700
by a watch officer in the White House Situation Room,

292
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:54,500
and it calls the threat unfounded.

293
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:59,620
But it also records that the director of the Situation Room disputes that account.

294
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:02,480
So the report does not say the words were never spoken.

295
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:04,180
It says the threat was unfounded,

296
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,520
and that there is an argument about how it started.

297
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:10,180
And one thing that gets the order of events backwards.

298
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:14,380
The threat arrived after the decision not to return to Washington had already been taken.

299
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:16,280
It did not cause the diversion.

300
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:18,920
The president wanted to go home.

301
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:23,980
He said so, repeatedly. And he was overruled by people whose job was to keep him alive.

302
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:28,760
So instead, the aeroplane went to Barksdale Air Force Base in Louisiana.

303
00:16:29,270 --> 00:16:31,200
It landed there at about a quarter to twelve.

304
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:34,800
And from a room with portraits of airmen on the wall,

305
00:16:35,220 --> 00:16:36,920
he spoke to the country a second time.

306
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:40,220
Freedom itself was attacked this morning.

307
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:45,260
Then on again, west, to Offutt Air Force Base in Nebraska,

308
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:49,460
where the United States Strategic Command keeps a bunker 40 feet underground.

309
00:16:49,900 --> 00:16:52,240
He landed there just before three in the afternoon.

310
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:55,400
A note on the times for those last legs.

311
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:58,880
The commission gives far fewer of them than the retellings do.

312
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:03,560
We could not source the departure minutes from Barksdale or Offutt to a primary document,

313
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:05,640
so we are not going to state them as fact.

314
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:09,800
By the evening, the airspace over the United States was empty.

315
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:11,800
A complete closure had been ordered,

316
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:13,640
and by around quarter past twelve,

317
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:17,240
every commercial and general aviation aircraft in the country was on the ground.

318
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:22,300
Air Force One flew the last leg home almost alone in American airspace,

319
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,740
which is what it had been for most of the day anyway.

320
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:29,580
What the record says. Strip out the argument,

321
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:32,300
and what is left is a sequence that nobody designed.

322
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:36,100
A request for fighter escort made at 959,

323
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,200
answered at about half past eleven.

324
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,760
In order to shoot down a civilian airliner,

325
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:44,920
given by a man the chain of command does not run through,

326
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:47,060
about an aeroplane that had already crashed.

327
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:51,840
A confirmation call whose existence the board could not document,

328
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:56,080
from a room where two other people were writing everything down and recorded no such

329
00:17:56,080 --> 00:18:01,260
call. An authority that reached the defense command 28 minutes too late,

330
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,180
and reached the pilots not at all.

331
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:05,800
None of this is a conspiracy.

332
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:07,680
All of it is in the report,

333
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,600
in the notes, and on the tapes,

334
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:12,160
and it has been public for more than twenty years.

335
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:14,920
Almost all of it got fixed.

336
00:18:15,380 --> 00:18:19,440
Not by an inquiry, but because the people inside it could see what had happened while

337
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:24,580
it was happening. The rules for who can authorize engaging a civilian aircraft were

338
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:29,100
written down. The link between the Civil Aviation Authority and the military was rebuilt

339
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:31,820
so that a hijacking reaches a defense sector in minutes,

340
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:37,000
not never. The board's own summary of the morning is four words long,

341
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:39,040
and it is not about any individual.

342
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:43,600
Improvised. Untested. Unfamiliar.

343
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:49,120
Unprepared. The forty people on United 93 did not know any of that.

344
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:51,340
They took a vote, and they went up the aisle,

345
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:53,500
and they brought the aeroplane down themselves.

346
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:57,840
The system that was supposed to protect them never knew they were there.

347
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:01,820
If the part that stays with you is an order that went nowhere,

348
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:06,100
we made the film about the tapes that proved the military's own timeline was wrong.

349
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:09,060
The tapes that broke NORAD's 9 -11 story,

350
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,460
right here on this channel.

351
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:13,680
And subscribe to Black Box Breakdown so you don't miss the next one.

352
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:16,320
If this one got under your skin a little,

353
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:21,760
good. That's the point. And it only keeps happening because people like you keep showing

354
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:23,940
up. So do one thing for me.

355
